---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.2 · Quest Infrastructure" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-2" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Quest Infrastructure</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Use the cash and house teleports from 2.1 to open useful quest areas and transport. Prepare for one quest, finish it, bank, then move to the next.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Finish the kingdom, Lunar, Recipe for Disaster and later elf-chain prerequisites that are useful now: Dragon Slayer I, Underground Pass, Shilo Village, the Dorgesh-Kaan chain, Between a Rock, Heroes' Quest and Monkey Madness I. Reach 50 Smithing and 50 Mining along the way. Family Crest is already complete from 1.4."
        stats={["50 Smithing before Between a Rock", "50 Mining before Heroes' Quest", "Your roughly 40 Herblore is enough for this chapter", "Quest rewards improve Attack, Strength and Defence"]}
        unlocks={["Upgraded Iban's staff banked", "Shilo Village and Dorgesh-Kaan access", "Dorgesh-Kaan–Keldagrim train and Tears of Guthix", "Heroes' Guild / Throne of Miscellania prerequisite", "Ape Atoll progression and dragon scimitar purchase access"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Quests you have already completed:</strong> Chapter 1 finished Shield of Arrav, Lost City, Merlin's Crystal, Jungle Potion, The Lost Tribe, The Giant Dwarf, The Dig Site, Dwarf Cannon, Fishing Contest, Biohazard, The Grand Tree, Tree Gnome Village and <strong>Family Crest</strong>. Keep its steel gauntlets: Avan can turn them into <strong>goldsmith gauntlets</strong> for much better gold-smelting XP if you later choose that Smithing method. It also finished Ernest the Chicken, Animal Magnetism and the relevant Barbarian Training foundation. Dragon Slayer I was only <em>started</em> in 1.4 for the anti-dragon shield; this page finishes it. Bring the 2.1 house tablets and ordinary teleport jewellery for banking between quests, not every reserved Chapter 1 item at once.</div>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Smithing and Dragon Slayer I</div>
        <h2>Reach 50 Smithing, then finish Dragon Slayer I.</h2>
      </section>

      <RouteStep id="i22-smithing-50" number="1" title="Reach 50 Smithing for Between a Rock">
        <p><strong>Why 50:</strong> the gold helmet in Between a Rock needs 50 Smithing. You will be around 42 after Chapter 1; check your skill tab and train to <strong>50 without a boost</strong>. Keep four gold bars for Between a Rock and leave your Construction and quest bars banked while training.</p>
        <p><strong>Recommended: Giants' Foundry.</strong> Sleeping Giants in 1.2 already unlocked Kovac's workshop under the Giants' Plateau east of Al Kharid; a ring of dueling to Emir's Arena or the Giants' Foundry minigame teleport gets you close. Check the Wintertodt/Tempoross ore and bar bank first. Bring metal bars or unwanted smithable metal equipment, plus a bucket or ice gloves; the workshop has a bank. A straightforward early sword uses <strong>14 iron and 14 steel bars</strong>. Smelt missing iron from iron ore and missing steel from one iron ore plus two coal each, using banked ore or ordinary mining/shop stock. Do not sacrifice the steel bars set aside for Mahogany Homes and later quest supplies.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Ask <strong>Kovac</strong> for a commission and pick moulds matching its two descriptive words.</li>
          <li>Put <strong>28 bars' worth</strong> of usable metal into the crucible, pour the preform, then follow the temperature bar through the hammer, grind and polish stations. Cool or heat the sword when the interface calls for it; working at the wrong temperature damages quality.</li>
          <li>Hand the finished sword to Kovac for Smithing XP, coins and reputation. Repeat with banked iron/steel until the skill tab shows <strong>50</strong>; save spare reputation and metal for the later 70-Smithing block.</li>
        </ol>
        <TrainingOptions id="i22-smithing-methods" informational={true} skill="Smithing" target="50, unboosted" why="Between a Rock needs 50 Smithing now. You will return to Smithing for Song of the Elves later." recommended="Giants' Foundry with banked iron/steel is resource-efficient and pays back coins. A 14/14 mix is a simple recipe to learn with; stop when you reach 50." relaxed="Use ordinary bars at an anvil if you prefer less minigame attention; check the bank first and make only enough items to reach 50." fast="Blast Furnace can process banked ore faster, but do not buy an oversized gold-ore stock solely to replace this short checkpoint." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i22-dragon-slayer" number="2" title="Finish Dragon Slayer I and keep the anti-dragon shield">
        <p><strong>Prerequisite:</strong> the Champions' Guild's 32 Quest Points were earned in Chapter 1, and 1.4 started Dragon Slayer I to obtain the anti-dragon shield for dragon bones. Continue from the shield stage shown in your journal. This completion supplies the missing Heroes' Quest prerequisite and awards <strong>18,650 Strength and 18,650 Defence XP</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Bank check:</strong> get <strong>three regular planks, 90 steel nails, a hammer and 2,000 coins</strong> for the ship; an <strong>unfired bowl, one Wizard's mind bomb, lobster pot and silk</strong> for the map pieces; and either Telekinetic Grab runes with a suitable attack or another <strong>10,000 coins</strong> for Wormbrain's piece. Keep the anti-dragon shield from Duke Horacio, food, a teleport and combat runes/gear. Buy missing nails from the Varrock sawmill operator, a lobster pot at a fishing shop, and a mind bomb at the Falador or Burthorpe pub; make an unfired bowl from soft clay at a pottery wheel if the bank lacks one.</p>
        <p>Resolve the three map pieces, repair the ship at Port Sarim and sail to Crandor. For <strong>Elvarg</strong>, equip the anti-dragon shield, use your 43 Prayer and bring prayer restoration and strong food; Magic or Ranged is reasonable if you have not done much melee training. Unlock the Karamja Volcano passage before leaving so a failed attempt is easier to recover. Finish with Oziach, retain the shield, and check your new Defence level. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dragon_Slayer_I" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki map-piece and fight details</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace missing map and ship supplies before leaving the bank">
          <p><strong>Replace any missing supplies:</strong> ordinary logs become <strong>regular planks</strong> for 100 coins each at the Varrock sawmill; its operator also sells steel nails and saws. Buy silk from the silk trader in Al Kharid, a lobster pot from Gerrant in Port Sarim, and the mind bomb from Falador's Rising Sun. Mine clay at Rimmington, soften it with water, then use the pottery wheel there to make the <strong>unfired bowl</strong> at 8 Crafting; do not put this bowl in the oven.</p>
          <p><strong>Reusable quest supplies:</strong> Lumbridge's general store sells buckets, pots, tinderboxes, chisels, hammers and shears; the knife in Lumbridge castle's kitchen and the spade in Falador's estate-agent building are free replacements. Buy rope from Ned in Draynor, and needles/thread and jewellery moulds from Dommik in Al Kharid. Shear a sheep and spin the wool at Lumbridge castle whenever a later quest needs another ball of wool.</p>
          <p><strong>Bars and glass:</strong> buy only missing copper, tin, iron, coal and gold ore from Ordan in Keldagrim's Blast Furnace shop. A regular furnace smelts bronze from one copper + one tin, steel from one iron + two coal, and gold from one gold ore; iron ore can fail to smelt, so continue until you have the required number of iron bars. Buy a bucket of sand and soda ash from a charter-ship trader, such as Port Khazard, and smelt them together for one new molten glass. A glassblowing pipe from the charter trader makes later glass items; make fresh glass for these quest items, since the 1,590 Earth orbs were used for battlestaves in 2.1.</p>
          <p><strong>Wormbrain and the fight:</strong> the cheaper map option needs a way to kill Wormbrain plus <strong>one law and one air rune</strong> for Telekinetic Grab. Buy the air rune from Aubury in Varrock and the law rune from the Wizards' Guild in Yanille. Guild entry needs current 66 Magic; use the Chapter 2.1 mind-bomb access method if your base level is lower. Aubury also stocks mind, chaos and death runes for combat. Replace a missing anti-dragon shield through Duke Horacio before fighting Elvarg. Check your food, runes and potion doses for this trip; use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> if the bank is short.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Western passage and southern Karamja</div>
        <h2>Open the way to Tirannwn and Shilo Village.</h2>
      </section>

      <RouteStep id="i22-underground-pass" number="3" title="Finish Underground Pass and upgrade Iban's staff">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Underground Pass is the route's doorway to Regicide and the later elf line, and its staff becomes a useful midgame Magic weapon. Biohazard is complete and the <strong>25 Ranged</strong> gate is already exceeded. Start with King Lathas in Ardougne, then set aside a session for the pass.</p>
        <p><strong>Withdraw:</strong> <strong>two or more ropes</strong>, a normal bow with a few <strong>non-poisoned metal-tipped arrows</strong>, spade, a regular plank, bucket, tinderbox, food, prayer/energy supplies, light combat gear, a teleport out and room for quest items. Your roughly 51 Agility helps but does not eliminate failed obstacles. Bank before entry and bring extra food rather than trying to save every slot. If the obstacles become frustrating, restock or return another session. You can continue at your current Agility level.</p>
        <p>Finish Iban and collect <strong>Iban's staff</strong>, then visit the <strong>Dark Mage in West Ardougne</strong> with <strong>200,000 coins</strong> to upgrade it to <strong>Iban's staff (u)</strong> and its <strong>2,500-charge</strong> capacity. Bank the staff. It requires <strong>50 Attack and 50 Magic to wield</strong>; You have the Magic level, but may still be below 50 Attack. Bank the staff until you can wield it; the Attack reward selected for Monkey Madness I later on this page will help. Underground Pass also gives <strong>3,000 Attack and 3,000 Agility XP</strong>; check your levels after claiming it. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Underground_Pass" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki obstacle and Iban walkthrough</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Pack the pass's small tools as well as its combat inventory">
          <p><strong>Bank check:</strong> the plank, bucket and tinderbox can be obtained inside the pass, but bringing one of each avoids relying on a later pickup. Use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> for these and Ned for replacement ropes. Lowe's Archery Emporium in Varrock sells a normal bow and plain bronze arrows; take a small spare stack because the fire-arrow obstacle can need another attempt. Ogre, training and composite bows are unsuitable here.</p>
          <p>Recheck <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> and carry enough food for failed obstacles. The 200,000-coin staff upgrade is a separate purchase after the quest; do not spend its reserved coins on bulk supplies.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i22-shilo" number="4" title="Complete Shilo Village and open the village/cart route">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Shilo is a prerequisite for Lunar Diplomacy's quest chain and Sir Amik's Recipe for Disaster step, as well as a useful southern Karamja bank/cart destination. <strong>Jungle Potion</strong> was finished in 1.3; the <strong>20 Crafting and 32 Agility</strong> checks are already passed. Reach Mosol Rei outside Shilo with fairy ring <strong>CKR</strong> and the dramen staff, or use a gnome glider and walk.</p>
        <p><strong>Bring:</strong> <strong>one spade, one rope, one chisel, one lit torch or candle</strong> (that light is consumed), <strong>one bronze wire</strong> and <strong>three ordinary bones</strong>. Jiminua's store near Tai Bwo Wannai sells the torch and small tools. If no bronze wire remains, smith one bronze bar into wire at a normal anvil before travelling; this needs only 4 Smithing. Bones can be obtained during the quest, but banking three first avoids accidentally burying the last one. Add antipoison, food, prayer restoration, a teleport and Magic/Ranged gear.</p>
        <p>Finish the temple and tomb sequence, then fight <strong>Nazastarool's three forms</strong> (roughly level 91/68/93). Use the dolmen as a safespot with Magic or Ranged if your melee levels are low; fire spells or Crumble Undead are good choices. Bank between phases/trips when the quest permits. Keep the <strong>beads of the dead</strong> until the quest is complete, then verify Shilo entry and cart travel. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Shilo_Village" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki tomb map and Nazastarool positions</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover a consumed light, wire and ordinary bones">
          <p>Buy a <strong>torch from Jiminua</strong> and light it with your tinderbox; the quest consumes this light, so do not substitute the enclosed lantern reserved for later caves. Make the bronze bar from one copper and one tin ore using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a>, then use a hammer at the Varrock west-bank anvil to make wire. Kill three chickens or other low-level creatures that drop <strong>ordinary bones</strong>, and bank them without burying them.</p>
          <p>Check antipoison, prayer doses, food and combat runes before the tomb trip; the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> gives a refill path when earlier quests used the last bottles.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Dorgesh-Kaan chain</div>
        <h2>Open the cave-goblin city, its weekly XP utility and its railway.</h2>
        <p><strong>Dorgesh-Kaan</strong> is the cave-goblin city beneath Lumbridge, reached through the castle cellar/Dorgeshuun mine after The Lost Tribe. The three quests below open its city, nearby minigame and railway. Finish and rebank after each.</p>
      </section>

      <RouteStep id="i22-death-dorgeshuun" number="5" title="Complete Death to the Dorgeshuun and enter the cave-goblin city">
        <p><strong>The Lost Tribe</strong>, Goblin Diplomacy and Rune Mysteries are already complete; 23 Agility/Thieving are far below your current levels. In the Lumbridge castle cellar, go through the rear cave to Mistag. Bring a <strong>safe enclosed light source</strong>, tinderbox, pickaxe, food and Magic/melee gear. The quest needs <strong>two full seven-piece H.A.M. outfits</strong> (hood, shirt, robe, logo, cloak, gloves, boots). Check the bank from the earlier H.A.M. work; pickpocket members at the hideout east of Draynor for missing pieces after starting the quest, when the outfit chance improves.</p>
        <p>Show Zanik the surface and finish the H.A.M. investigation, then return with a pickaxe and light for the swamp-cave section. Use prayer, food and a teleport; open flames are unsafe in gas pockets. At the final mill fight, handle the guards before <strong>Sigmund</strong> and switch from a protected style as Zanik attacks. Complete the quest before moving on: it gives <strong>2,000 Thieving and 2,000 Ranged XP</strong> and opens <strong>Dorgesh-Kaan</strong> and the H.A.M. storeroom. Leave the rich-chest diary task for later unless you already have 78 Thieving. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Death_to_the_Dorgeshuun" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Zanik route and cave map</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the cave light before Dorgesh-Kaan is open">
          <p>If the old mining helmet or lantern is missing, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-3/#i13-quest-supplies`}> enclosed-lantern recipe</a> to make and fuel an oil lantern before entering. Dorgesh-Kaan's lamp shop opens after this quest, so it cannot supply this first trip. Keep a tinderbox for relighting and do not carry an open candle into gas.</p>
          <p>Count <strong>two complete H.A.M. sets</strong>, not fourteen assorted pieces. Start the quest first, then pickpocket H.A.M. members until every missing piece is present; check each of the seven pieces for both outfits.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i22-tears-guthix" number="6" title="Complete Tears of Guthix and retain the sapphire lantern">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> the short quest unlocks the weekly Tears of Guthix minigame, which gives XP to whichever skill is lowest when you play. The <strong>43 Quest Points, 49 Firemaking, 20 Crafting and 20 Mining</strong> checks are already met. Before entering the Lumbridge Swamp Caves, prepare a <strong>lit sapphire lantern</strong>: check for a bullseye lantern already banked, or buy an empty one from <strong>Miltog's Lamps</strong> in the Dorgesh-Kaan market opened in Step 5. Get <strong>one swamp tar</strong> from Lumbridge Swamp; use it on the lamp still beside Miltog, then use the lantern on the still to fill it. Use a <strong>cut sapphire</strong> on the lantern to replace its lens, and light it with a tinderbox. Keep an ordinary enclosed light too. Keep the removed lens so the lantern can be converted again later.</p>
        <p>Bring <strong>rope, pickaxe, chisel, tinderbox, food, antipoison and a teleport</strong>; the cave has aggressive monsters and a water crossing that can extinguish a light. Reach <strong>Juna</strong> in the Chasm of Tears from the swamp caves/Dorgeshuun mine, use the sapphire lantern on a light creature, mine the magic stone, chisel the stone bowl and return to Juna. Bank the sapphire lantern afterward: Lunar Diplomacy can reuse its lantern body, and later quests may need it again. Visit for weekly tears when you feel like it; you can complete this chapter without them. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Tears_of_Guthix" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki light-creature and bowl details</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare one sapphire and a filled lantern">
          <p>If the sapphire has already been used, buy an uncut one from Ardougne's gem trader when stock is available, or mine Shilo Village's surface gem rocks and cut gems until you have <strong>one cut sapphire</strong>. The number of rocks needed will vary. Bring the chisel and leave your other quest gems banked.</p>
          <p>The empty lantern from Miltog still needs oil: collect one swamp tar from the Lumbridge Swamp ground, process it in the lamp still, fill the lantern, fit the sapphire and light it. Keep the Chapter 1 enclosed light as your spare; <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-3/#i13-quest-supplies`}> enclosed-lantern recipe</a> covers rebuilding it. Keep the lantern for Lunar Diplomacy and leave any extra sapphires for later jewellery.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i22-another-slice" number="7" title="Complete Another Slice of H.A.M. and open the Keldagrim train">
        <p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Death to the Dorgeshuun just finished; The Giant Dwarf and The Dig Site were completed in 1.3; <strong>15 Attack and 25 Prayer</strong> are already covered. Bring an enclosed light, a tinderbox, one rope if the Lumbridge Swamp entrance is not already roped, food, a teleport and <strong>Magic or Ranged gear</strong>—the final two level-30 enemies cannot be dealt with using melee. Leave at least <strong>eight free inventory slots</strong> for artefacts. The trowel and specimen brush are provided during the quest.</p>
        <p>Start in Dorgesh-Kaan, excavate and clean the artefacts, then finish Zanik's investigation and the fight with Sigmund. The city-to-<strong>Keldagrim railway</strong> is the useful transport payoff; the quest also gives the ancient mace, <strong>3,000 Mining and 3,000 Prayer XP</strong>. Check your Mining XP before training the Heroes' Quest gap in Step 9. A moving-over-distance sphere from Oldak can later return you to Dorgesh-Kaan; use one when it would save you a journey. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Another_Slice_of_H.A.M." target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki artefact and fight details</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover small cave supplies before the excavation">
          <p>Reuse the lit enclosed lantern from Steps 5–6. If it was lost, Miltog now sells a replacement bullseye lantern and the adjacent still converts Lumbridge swamp tar into its oil. Bring a tinderbox and buy a rope from Ned if your chosen swamp entrance still needs one. The excavation's trowel and specimen brush are collected from the quest workers; they are not an extra Dig Site shopping requirement.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Dwarven quests and the Heroes' Guild</div>
        <h2>Claim the quest rewards before finishing 50 Mining.</h2>
      </section>

      <RouteStep id="i22-between-rock" number="8" title="Complete Between a Rock with 50 Smithing">
        <p><strong>Dwarf Cannon and Fishing Contest</strong> were finished in 1.2. Check <strong>30 Defence, 40 Mining and 50 Smithing</strong> before starting; Chapter 1 already brought Defence and Mining above the first two requirements. Travel to Keldagrim via the new Dorgesh-Kaan train or the normal mine-cart route, then speak to <strong>Dondakan</strong> at the mine outside the city.</p>
        <p><strong>Withdraw or obtain:</strong> <strong>four gold bars</strong> (smelt missing bars from gold ore, or use the bank), a <strong>hammer, pickaxe and ammo mould</strong>, at least <strong>1,000 coins</strong> for travel, a teleport, food and combat gear. Nulodion near the Dwarf Cannon start sells an ammo mould if yours is missing. The quest turns one gold bar into a cannonball and three into a gold helmet; reserve all four rather than discovering a shortage mid-story. Bring protection/healing for the Arzinian mine fight, and follow the schematic dialogue/puzzle in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Between_a_Rock..." target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Between a Rock walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p>Finish the quest and bank the <strong>gold helmet</strong>; it opens the Arzinian gold mine if you want that resource later. The completion rewards <strong>5,000 Mining, Smithing and Defence XP each</strong>. These rewards plus Another Slice's 3,000 Mining XP are why the route waits until now to train Mining to 50. Check your Defence level after this reward and Dragon Slayer I so you know how much training remains for later quests.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make sure you have four gold bars for the quest">
          <p>Count four finished gold bars now. If the bank is short, buy the missing gold ore from Ordan and smelt it at any regular furnace (40 Smithing), using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a>. Four means <strong>one for the cannonball plus three for the helmet</strong>; set them aside before making any more jewellery.</p>
          <p>Nulodion supplies the ammo mould if the Dwarf Cannon one is gone. Keep the travel coins, a charged teleport, food and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> separate from the helmet materials.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i22-mining-50" number="9" title="Reach 50 Mining for Heroes' Quest">
        <p>Read your skill tab after the <strong>3,000 Mining XP</strong> from Another Slice and <strong>5,000</strong> from Between a Rock. Chapter 1 left you around 44 Mining; train from your new level to <strong>unboosted 50</strong> for Heroes' Quest. Stop there for now. Later steps cover <strong>52 Mining for full Legends' Quest</strong> and 60 for Lunar Diplomacy.</p>
        <p>Take the <strong>2,000 stardust</strong> Chapter 1 reserved to <strong>Dusuri's Star Shop</strong> and buy the <strong>celestial ring</strong> if you have not already. Its invisible +4 Mining boost helps success rate but <em>does not satisfy</em> Heroes' Quest's level check. If you already bought the ring, you can return to Shooting Stars for relaxed Mining XP without saving another 2,000 stardust.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i22-mining-methods" informational={true} skill="Mining" target="50, unboosted" why="Heroes' Quest requires 50 Mining. Later quests give Mining XP before you return for the higher levels." recommended="Shooting Stars: inspect the telescope or community star notice, travel to a landed star you can mine, and click its layers until it disappears or you want a break. Extra stardust may buy later shop rewards, but there is no new 2,000-dust quota." relaxed="Motherlode Mine beneath Falador: mine pay-dirt veins, deposit it in the hopper, collect ores from the sack and bank them. It is available from 30 Mining and feeds later Smithing. Calcified rocks are another low-attention option only if you already opened Cam Torum through Perilous Moons; that side quest is not required here." fast="Mine iron or use another active method if you want the last levels quickly; sandstone/granite are not the default merely for speed." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i22-heroes" number="10" title="Complete Heroes' Quest with a current co-op partner">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Heroes' Quest is the remaining direct prerequisite for <strong>Throne of Miscellania</strong> in 2.3, and it also feeds Sir Amik/Legends later. Check <strong>55 Quest Points, 53 Cooking, 53 Fishing, 25 Herblore and unboosted 50 Mining</strong>. Chapter 1 already supplied Shield of Arrav, Lost City and Merlin's Crystal; Step 2 finished Dragon Slayer I. Check that each is marked complete in your journal.</p>
        <p>Start with Achietties outside the Heroes' Guild between Burthorpe and Taverley. For the lava eel, withdraw the <strong>one harralander reserved in 1.3</strong>, <strong>one vial of water</strong> and a <strong>normal fishing rod</strong>. Get blamish snail slime through the quest, make the harralander potion (unf), add the slime, then oil the rod. Obtain a dusty key for Taverley Dungeon if you lack the 70-Agility shortcut, and bring fishing bait, food, antipoison and a teleport. Cook the caught eel. For Entrana, get <strong>ice gloves</strong> from the Ice Queen if you do not have them; bring a pickaxe, combat supplies and food for that trip, then bank prohibited gear before travelling to Entrana for the fire feather. Keep the gloves afterward.</p>
        <p><strong>Partner check:</strong> the current quest still needs a player from the <em>opposite Shield of Arrav gang</em> for the Master Thieves' Armband section; Ironmen also need a partner for this part. Check your quest journal for your gang, then use the in-game <strong>Grouping → Shield of Arrav</strong> channel to find the opposite side. A player who already completed Heroes' Quest can still help. Follow the Brimhaven mansion, key and candlestick steps for your gang together. Finish with Achietties and bank the ice gloves and oily fishing rod. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Heroes%27_Quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki gang-specific steps and dungeon map</a>.</p>
        <p>The quest gives about <strong>3,075 Attack, Strength, Defence and Hitpoints XP</strong> each, plus smaller skill rewards. Check your new levels before choosing what to train next.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Check your gang's disguise and replace spent eel supplies">
          <p><strong>Black Arm Gang:</strong> bring a <strong>black full helm, black platebody and black platelegs</strong>. Valaine in the Champions' Guild sells the helm and legs; Horvik's armour shop in Varrock sells the body. Use these exact three armour pieces; black robes and a med helm do not work. <strong>Phoenix Gang:</strong> bring Ranged or Magic to kill the target through the mansion window. Keep any black armour for King's Ransom.</p>
          <p>If the reserved harralander is gone, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> to obtain another clean herb and vial of water. Gerrant's Port Sarim fishing shop supplies the normal rod, bait and, after the quest conversation, <strong>blamish snail slime</strong>. Combine harralander with the vial of water, add the slime, and apply the resulting oil to the rod.</p>
          <p>Without the 70-Agility shortcut, kill Taverley Dungeon's jailer for his jail key and free <strong>Velrak the explorer</strong> to obtain a dusty key. The Ice Queen is under White Wolf Mountain: bring a pickaxe for the 50-Mining rock obstacle, food and combat supplies. Keep her ice gloves for the fire-feather task and later quests.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Ape Atoll and the combat-reward decision</div>
        <h2>Unlock the dragon scimitar and collect useful combat XP.</h2>
      </section>

      <RouteStep id="i22-monkey-madness" number="11" title="Complete Monkey Madness I and take Daero's Attack/Defence reward">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> The Grand Tree and Tree Gnome Village are complete from Chapter 1. Monkey Madness I opens Ape Atoll progression, the <strong>dragon scimitar purchase</strong> and the Awowogei Recipe for Disaster prerequisite in 2.4. You can attempt the quest without training all three melee skills to 65 first. Talk to King Narnode in the Grand Tree, finish this quest, and only then collect the chosen XP from Daero.</p>
        <p><strong>Check or gather:</strong> <strong>one gold bar, a ball of wool and five free inventory slots</strong> for bananas you pick from the Ape Atoll garden during the quest, plus room for Karamjan monkey bones/corpse and other quest items. A gold bar may remain from The Dig Site or can be smelted from ore; kill a regular monkey on Karamja for its bones if you do not already have them. Take anti-poison, several prayer potions, strong food, energy restoration, a teleport and gear for Magic or Ranged. Rebank before each dangerous Ape Atoll/tunnel section. Use <strong>Protect from Melee</strong> where the monkeys swarm; take particular care if your Defence is still close to the roughly 34 reached in Chapter 1. The <strong>Jungle Demon</strong> can be fought from a safer ranged/magic position with prayers and food. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_I" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki greegree, tunnel and boss details</a>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Daero reward choice for this route:</strong> choose <strong>35,000 XP each in Attack and Defence</strong> and <strong>20,000 XP each in Strength and Hitpoints</strong>. Dragon Slayer I and Heroes already added Strength/Defence XP; this choice helps you reach <strong>50 Attack</strong> for the upgraded Iban's staff and toward the later <strong>60/65/70 Defence</strong> requirements. Starting around Chapter 1's 46 Attack, Underground Pass + Heroes + this 35,000-XP choice clear the level-50 Attack threshold, but <strong>check your level</strong> before equipping the staff. You will still need <strong>130 Attack+Strength</strong> for the Warriors' Guild and 70 Defence for Piety; 2.5 includes training for both.</div>
        <p>The dragon scimitar is now <strong>available to buy</strong> from Daga on Ape Atoll, but needs <strong>60 Attack to wield</strong>. Buy one when you have the coins and level to use it. Keep your greegree and other useful quest items for Awowogei's later return to the island.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace the amulet materials and prepare for the tunnels">
          <p>Smelt <strong>one fresh gold bar</strong> from Ordan's gold ore if Between a Rock used the last four. Shear one sheep and spin its wool at Lumbridge castle for the ball of wool; the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> also covers missing moulds and tools. Obtain Karamjan monkey bones by killing a normal monkey on Karamja before travelling, and collect the five bananas in the quest garden.</p>
          <p><strong>Lost M'speak amulet:</strong> collect new <strong>monkey dentures from the stacked crates in the house south of Marim's marketplace</strong>. Search that house's south-east crate to enter the cavern, then the north-west crate for the <strong>M'amulet mould</strong>. Take dentures, mould and a fresh gold bar to <strong>Zooknock at the end of the southern Ape Atoll tunnel</strong>. Take his enchanted bar and the returned mould to the <strong>wall of flame beneath the Temple of Marimbo</strong>, make the unstrung amulet, and add one ball of wool. This same process replaces an amulet after the quest.</p>
          <p>The first monkey talisman comes from the monkey child during this quest. Keep the finished <strong>M'speak amulet and Karamjan monkey greegree</strong> for Awowogei. Refill prayer and antipoison via the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> and bank between dangerous trips; check how many doses remain after each trip.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <ExpandableNote label="Later quests" title="What can wait until later chapters">
        <p><strong>Family Crest is already complete in 1.4.</strong> Haunted Mine and its salve amulet belong with the undead-heavy Morytania/combat work in 2.5; its difficult Treus Dayth fight need not interrupt the kingdom/Lunar prerequisites. Black Knights' Fortress, Recruitment Drive and Wanted! are saved for the King's Ransom/Proselyte path when those rewards matter. Ghosts Ahoy, Big Chompy Bird Hunting and RFD-specific errands are covered alongside the relevant quests in 2.4–2.5. Temple of the Eye, Enakhra's Lament, Spirits of the Elid, Icthlarin's Little Helper, Contact!, Scorpion Catcher and Zogre Flesh Eaters can all wait; none is needed to begin 2.3.</p>
        <p><strong>Legends' Quest:</strong> Sir Amik's RFD step requires <em>starting</em> Legends and entering the Kharazi Jungle, not completing it. In 2.4, check the <strong>107 Quest Points</strong> and start it when Sir Amik needs access. Finish the full quest later in Chapter 2, once you have 45 Herblore and 52 Mining, and use its selectable XP rewards on <strong>Herblore</strong>. You can leave both levels until those later steps.</p>
        <p>The Dorgesh-Kaan <strong>78-Thieving rich chest</strong> is also deferred; you can leave it for later whether or not you tried Piscarilius artefacts in 2.1.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">2.2 exit check</div>
        <h3>You can start the kingdom and the next quest chains.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Dragon Slayer I, Underground Pass, Shilo Village, Death to the Dorgeshuun, Tears of Guthix, Another Slice of H.A.M., Between a Rock, Heroes' Quest and Monkey Madness I</strong> complete. Family Crest remains complete from 1.4.</li>
          <li><strong>50 Smithing and 50 Mining</strong> reached without boosts. Your 40+ Herblore from Chapter 1 is enough for the next quests.</li>
          <li><strong>Iban's staff (u)</strong>, anti-dragon shield, ice gloves, sapphire lantern, gold helmet, useful quest items and house tablets banked; Shilo, Dorgesh-Kaan, its Keldagrim train and Ape Atoll opened. Dragon scimitar purchase access is unlocked; its 60-Attack wield requirement is a later checkpoint.</li>
          <li><strong>Daero reward claimed:</strong> 35,000 Attack/Defence and 20,000 Strength/Hitpoints XP. Check your combat levels before wielding Iban's staff; later steps cover the Warriors' Guild, King's Ransom and Piety requirements.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Next, 2.3 can begin <strong>Throne of Miscellania</strong> using Heroes' Quest and the Chapter 1 Fremennik Trials. Royal Trouble needs <strong>40 Slayer</strong>, so 2.3 includes training from the roughly 20 reached in Chapter 1. Lunar Diplomacy and Recipe for Disaster have their Shilo, Heroes, Underground Pass and Monkey Madness prerequisites ready for 2.4.</p>
      </section>

